   573		Let $\mathfrak G$ be a nonlocal game, and let $\mathcal S$, $\mathcal S'$ be two strategies that are $\delta$-close in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:strategy-distance}, for some $\delta \in [0,1]$, and that use the same state $\ket{\psi}$. If either $\mathcal S$ or $\mathcal S'$ is projective, then
   574		\[
   575			\bigl| \operatorname{val}^*(\mathfrak G, \mathcal S) - \operatorname{val}^*(\mathfrak G, \mathcal S') \bigr| \le O(\delta^{1/2})\,.
